      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In patients with systemic sclerosis (SSc), gastrointestinal (GI) tract involvement is almost universal. Any segment of the GI tract from mouth to anus can be involved, and GI symptoms are a frequent cause of morbidity. In severe cases, GI tract involvement can progress to the point of malnutrition requiring parenteral nutrition. GI tract involvement in SSc contributes to disease-related mortality although mostly as a co-morbidity rather than direct cause of death. The review is intended to help address challenges in the assessment and treatment of GI tract involvement in SSc."},
